From a02f95f46719f804a4a3b043b16c19352375e01c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Francke <lars.francke@stackable.tech>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:41:34 +0100
Subject: PHOENIX-5215 Migrate from HTrace to OpenTelemetry tracing

Backport of apache/phoenix PR #2586
(https://github.com/apache/phoenix/pull/2586), squashed from its 14
commits (head cb3982a1a) and applied on top of the 5.3 line. The PR is
open against master and not merged at the time of this backport.

Removes Apache HTrace from Phoenix and replaces it with a thin
OpenTelemetry facade, PhoenixTracing, adapted from HBase's TraceUtil
(HBASE-22120). Phoenix compiles against opentelemetry-api 1.15.0 with
"provided" scope and relies on the OpenTelemetry API and SDK that HBase
ships; nothing is shaded. The HBase-table trace sink (PhoenixMetricsSink,
TraceWriter) is removed, TRACE ON/OFF still parse but no longer start a
Phoenix-side trace, and the phoenix.trace.* properties are deprecated and
no longer read. HTrace is banned as a direct dependency by
maven-enforcer.

Adaptations for 5.3.x compared to the master PR:

- UpdateStatisticsTool still passes htrace's SpanReceiver.class to
  TableMapReduceUtil.addDependencyJarsForClasses on this branch (master
  moved that list into PhoenixMapReduceUtil.addPhoenixDependencyJars,
  which does not exist here). The import and the class entry are dropped
  so htrace-core is no longer shipped to MapReduce containers, matching
  what the PR does in PhoenixMapReduceUtil on master.
- The PR's hunks for PhoenixMapReduceUtil.java and
  PhoenixMapReduceUtilTest.java only remove htrace references that are
  not present on this branch and are omitted.
- Dependency and RAT-exclusion context that only exists on master is not
  pulled in; only the OpenTelemetry additions are applied.

Co-authored-by: xavifeds8 <fernandisxavier8@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
